counterfactuals.output:
The KIMS CsI(Tl) search at the Yangyang Underground Laboratory found no statistically significant WIMP signal. For a WIMP mass near \(60\ \mathrm{GeV}/c^2\), it set 90% confidence-level upper limits of approximately:

- **Spin-independent WIMP–nucleon:**  
  \[
  \sigma_{\rm SI} < 3.1\times10^{-7}\ \mathrm{pb}
  \approx 3.1\times10^{-43}\ \mathrm{cm^2}
  \]

- **Spin-dependent WIMP–proton:**  
  \[
  \sigma_{\rm SD}^{p} < 4.3\times10^{-3}\ \mathrm{pb}
  \approx 4.3\times10^{-39}\ \mathrm{cm^2}
  \]

These limits, derived under standard Galactic-halo assumptions, strongly constrained WIMP interpretations of the DAMA annual-modulation signal, especially those involving scattering from iodine.
